<title>GERMANY: VW to sell 2 mln new Golfs - sources.</title>
<headline>VW to sell 2 mln new Golfs - sources.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Volkswagen AG plans to sell about two million of its new Golf cars a year in the medium term, company sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The sources said the new model will be priced as &quot;aggressively&quot; as VW's new Passat model, which was unveiled last year.</p>
<p>VW Chairman Ferdinand Piech said late on Monday that the company expected to sell 700,000 new Golfs in Europe in the first year of production.</p>
<p>VW produced 701,475 Golfs in 1996.</p>
<p>The carmaker was to introduce the new model in Bonn on Tuesday night.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
